de $\\lambda^t$. If $r=\\ln3$ is a characteristic root, which discrete mode corresponds to it?","options":["$(\\ln3)^t$","$\\mathrm{e}^{3t}$","$3^t$","$3t$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8b43d4574bd97ab1f35548dd","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_characteristic_equation_differential_equation_189635d0_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"The equation $x''-x'-2x=0$ has characteristic roots $2$ and $-1$, and every solution is $c_1\\mathrm{e}^{2t}+c_2\\mathrm{e}^{-t}$. Which solution satisfies $x(0)=3$ and $x'(0)=0$?","options":["$x(t)=2\\mathrm{e}^{2t}+\\mathrm{e}^{-t}$","$x(t)=\\mathrm{e}^{2t}+2\\mathrm{e}^{-t}$","$x(t)=3\\mathrm{e}^{2t}$","$x(t)=\\mathrm{e}^{2t}+2\\mathrm{e}^{t}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"76d3ce5270a3bda57696d17e","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"no_diagnostic_value"},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_characteristic_equation_differential_equation_189635d0_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For a homogeneous linear equation with constant coefficients and characteristic polynomial $p$, which statement about exponential solutions is correct?","options":["$\\mathrm{e}^{rt}$ solves it iff $p(r)=0$, so every solution is some $c\\mathrm{e}^{rt}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{rt}$ solves it whenever $p'(r)=0$, the critical points of $p$","$\\mathrm{e}^{rt}$ solves it iff $p(r)=0$, and $t\\mathrm{e}^{rt}$ solves it iff $p(r)=0$","$\\mathrm{e}^{rt}$ solves it iff $p(r)=0$, but not every solution is some $c\\mathrm{e}^{rt}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8decc2136d203384fa163145","time_limit":45,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"